  "id": "COMPOUND:13290 - PROTEIN:930",
  "verbalization": "Sodium aluminosilicate appears to be a target of multiple compounds that ultimately interact with the 5-hydroxytryptamine 3 receptor (5-HT3R). This relationship is mediated through the muscarinic acetylcholine receptor M5, which serves as a common intermediate in the pathways. The evidence suggests that Sodium aluminosilicate may influence the activity of muscarinic receptors, which in turn modulate the function of 5-HT3R. The presence of multiple distinct compounds—such as (+/-)-Pinoresinol and Brimonidine—each acting as targets of muscarinic receptors and ultimately targeting the 5-HT3R, indicates a potential mechanism involving receptor activation or modulation. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of muscarinic receptors in mediating the effects of these compounds on the 5-HT3R, suggesting a broader functional relationship between Sodium aluminosilicate and the 5-HT3R through receptor-based interactions.",
